.Dd October 8, 2026
.Dt MEDIA 4
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm media
.Nd Video4Linux2 compatible video device and media controller core
.Sh SYNOPSIS
To load the module at boot time, place the following lines in
.Xr loader.conf 5 :
.Bd -literal -offset indent
dmabuf_base_load="YES"
media_load="YES"
.Ed
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
module is a clean-room implementation of the Linux V4L2 and media controller user interfaces for
FreeBSD: video device nodes, a buffer queue, the controls framework, events, the media request API,
and a mem2mem scheduler.
Hardware drivers such as
.Xr cedrus 4
register with it and depend on it; applications written for Linux, such as FFmpeg's V4L2 request
hwaccel, work unchanged.
The interface headers are those of Linux (from the published user interface) and live in
.Pa sys/dev/media/uapi .
.Pp
The module depends on
.Sy dmabuf_base
.Pq Xr dmabuf 4 .
.Ss Device nodes
.Bl -tag -width ".Pa /dev/mediaN"
.It Pa /dev/videoN
A video device, one per registered driver function.
Mode 0660, owner root, group operator; see
.Xr devfs.rules 5
and
.Pa etc/devfs.rules
of the freebsd-media sources for giving group
.Dq video
access.
.It Pa /dev/mediaN
The media controller device of a driver; also the source of requests.
Same ownership.
.El
.Ss Video device ioctls
.Dv VIDIOC_QUERYCAP ,
.Dv VIDIOC_ENUM_FMT ,
.Dv VIDIOC_G_FMT ,
.Dv VIDIOC_S_FMT ,
.Dv VIDIOC_TRY_FMT ,
.Dv VIDIOC_ENUM_FRAMESIZES ,
.Dv VIDIOC_ENUM_FRAMEINTERVALS ,
.Dv VIDIOC_G_PARM ,
.Dv VIDIOC_S_PARM ,
.Dv VIDIOC_ENUMINPUT ,
.Dv VIDIOC_G_INPUT ,
.Dv VIDIOC_S_INPUT ,
.Dv VIDIOC_REQBUFS ,
.Dv VIDIOC_CREATE_BUFS ,
.Dv VIDIOC_QUERYBUF ,
.Dv VIDIOC_QBUF ,
.Dv VIDIOC_DQBUF ,
.Dv VIDIOC_PREPARE_BUF ,
.Dv VIDIOC_STREAMON ,
.Dv VIDIOC_STREAMOFF ,
.Dv VIDIOC_EXPBUF ,
.Dv VIDIOC_QUERYCTRL ,
.Dv VIDIOC_QUERY_EXT_CTRL ,
.Dv VIDIOC_QUERYMENU ,
.Dv VIDIOC_G_CTRL ,
.Dv VIDIOC_S_CTRL ,
.Dv VIDIOC_G_EXT_CTRLS ,
.Dv VIDIOC_S_EXT_CTRLS ,
.Dv VIDIOC_TRY_EXT_CTRLS ,
.Dv VIDIOC_G_PRIORITY ,
.Dv VIDIOC_S_PRIORITY ,
.Dv VIDIOC_SUBSCRIBE_EVENT ,
.Dv VIDIOC_UNSUBSCRIBE_EVENT ,
.Dv VIDIOC_DQEVENT .
.Pp
Buffers are memory-mapped (
.Dv V4L2_MEMORY_MMAP )
or imported dma-bufs
.Pq Dv V4L2_MEMORY_DMABUF ;
.Dv VIDIOC_EXPBUF
exports a mapped buffer as a
.Xr dmabuf 4
descriptor.
Orphaned buffers are supported: freeing a queue is not blocked by a mapping or an exported
descriptor.
.Ss Media controller ioctls
On
.Pa /dev/mediaN :
.Dv MEDIA_IOC_DEVICE_INFO ,
.Dv MEDIA_IOC_ENUM_ENTITIES ,
.Dv MEDIA_IOC_ENUM_LINKS ,
.Dv MEDIA_IOC_SETUP_LINK ,
.Dv MEDIA_IOC_G_TOPOLOGY ,
.Dv MEDIA_IOC_REQUEST_ALLOC .
On a request descriptor:
.Dv MEDIA_REQUEST_IOC_QUEUE ,
.Dv MEDIA_REQUEST_IOC_REINIT .
.Pp
The sub-device interface (v4l2-subdev) is not implemented.
.Ss Modules built on the core
.Bl -tag -width ".Sy vtest"
.It Xr cedrus 4
The Allwinner A64 video decoder.
.It Sy vtest
A virtual camera and a virtual mem2mem converter
.Pq Pa sys/modules/vtest ,
for testing the core with
.Xr v4l2-compliance 1
and for development without hardware.
Not built by default.
.El
.Sh SYSCTL VARIABLES AND TUNABLES
The core has none.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width ".Pa /dev/videoN"
.It Pa /dev/videoN
.It Pa /dev/mediaN
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr cedrus 4 ,
.Xr dmabuf 4 ,
.Xr v4l2_stateless 7
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Nm
core is part of the freebsd-media project, 2026.
It is not part of the FreeBSD base system.
